/*  What type an expression has — `InferTypeCore` and its helpers in
    `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.Core.cs`.

    Gives back the type as a node, `none` when there is nothing to go on (C#'s null), or a failure:
    the refusal, or `unsupported` for an expression this checker cannot type yet.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// What an expression's type is — with any written name of an interface resolved to it, as
    /// C#'s `InferType` resolves every type it hands back.
    Bind node or failure to infer unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define found as cast one's infer-core on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If cast one's mentions-interface on (found), return cast one's resolved on (found).
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind fact to mentions-interface unto checker, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
            Return (the entry for name in one's defs) is void and cast one's is-interface-name on (name).
        Done.
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            If inner's kind is not "atom" and cast one's mentions-interface on (inner), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-core unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "NumberLiteral", return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
        If kind is "StringLiteral", return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
        If kind is "BooleanLiteral", return cast plain-type on ("FactType").
        If kind is "BitsLiteral", return cast plain-type on ("BitsType").
        If kind is "VoidLiteral", return cast plain-type on ("VoidType").
        If kind is "VariableReference", return cast one's infer-name on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "UnaryExpression", return cast one's infer-unary on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "BinaryExpression", return cast one's infer-binary on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextJoin", return cast one's infer-join on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextConvert", return cast one's infer-text-convert on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "NumberConvert", return cast one's infer-number-convert on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "ButVoidDefault", return cast one's infer-but-void on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral", return cast one's infer-series-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SeriesAccess", return cast one's infer-series-access on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SeriesLength", return cast one's infer-series-length on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "CastExpression", return cast one's check-call on (said, true) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "FailureLiteral", return cast one's infer-failure-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "MapLiteral", return cast one's infer-map-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "MapLookup", return cast one's infer-map-lookup on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "MapHasKey" or kind is "MapHasEntry", return cast one's infer-map-has on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "FailureFallback", return cast one's infer-failure-fallback on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "FailurePropagate", return cast one's infer-failure-propagate on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "ObjectLiteral", return cast one's infer-object-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "PossessiveAccess", return cast one's infer-possessive on (said, false) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RecordNamedAccess", return cast one's infer-named-access on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RecordLiteral", return cast one's infer-record-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "IsTypeCheck", return cast one's infer-type-test on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "ConditionalExpression", return cast one's infer-conditional on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextSplit", return cast one's infer-text-split on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextContains", return cast one's infer-text-contains on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "LambdaLiteral", return cast one's infer-lambda on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextAffixTest", return cast one's infer-text-affix on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextFind", return cast one's infer-text-find on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextSubstringRange", return cast one's infer-text-range on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextSubstringEdge", return cast one's infer-text-edge on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextReplace", return cast one's infer-text-replace on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextCase", return cast one's infer-text-case on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextTrim", return cast one's infer-text-trim on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "BitsConvert", return cast one's infer-bits-convert on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "BitsShift", return cast one's infer-bits-shift on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "BitsAtWidth", return cast one's infer-bits-width on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RangeExpression", return cast one's infer-range on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SortExpression", return cast one's infer-sort on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RandomNumber", return cast one's infer-random-number on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RandomItem", return cast one's infer-random-item on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RandomlyShuffled", return cast one's infer-random-shuffled on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RandomGuess", return cast one's infer-random-guess on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "ChaseLiteral", return cast one's infer-chase-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SetLiteral", return cast one's infer-set-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SetHasMember", return cast one's infer-set-has on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "MatrixLiteral", return cast one's infer-matrix-literal on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "MatrixSized", return cast one's infer-matrix-sized on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "MatrixAccess", return cast one's infer-matrix-access on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "FileReadExpression", return cast one's infer-file-read on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "DirectoryContentsExpression", return cast one's infer-directory-contents on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "PathCheckExpression", return cast one's infer-path-check on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "RunExpression", return cast one's infer-run on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "PipeExpression", return cast one's infer-pipe on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "ReadExpression", return cast one's infer-read on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "EnvironmentVariableExpression", return cast one's infer-env-var on (said) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "CurrentDirectoryExpression", return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        If kind is "ProgramArgumentsExpression", return cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        If kind is "InterruptRequestedExpression", return cast plain-type on ("FactType").
        Return a failure (cast not-judged on (kind)).
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-none, given (the node shape):
        Return shape's kind is "none".
    Done.

    /// A type this checker cannot weigh yet — held behind `unsupported` wherever it turns up.
    Bind fact to beyond-types, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        If kind is "BookType":
            Return true.
        Done.
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            If inner's kind is not "atom" and inner's kind is not "list" and cast beyond-types on (inner), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    // ── Names ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to infer-name unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
        // ⚠ A narrowing is asked FIRST, before scope — C# keeps them by name, not by scope.
        Define narrowing as the entry for name in one's narrowed.
        If narrowing is not void, return narrowing.
        Define found as cast one's look-up on (name).
        If found is not void, return found's shape.
        If (the entry for name in one's hidden) is not void:
            Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "'{name}' is a top-level value, but function and method bodies can't see top-level data", "",
                at-row, "read '{name}' inside a top-level function or a method",
                "They see other functions (for mutual recursion) and top-level `permanently` constants, but not top-level data that can change. This keeps data flow explicit and prevents hidden mutation.\nDeclare it `Define {name} as <value> permanently.` if it never changes, or pass '{name}' in as a parameter, or define the function inside a scope where '{name}' is already bound, so it captures '{name}' as a closure.")).
        Done.
        Return cast one's unresolved on (said) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// A name nothing in scope defines — C#'s `NoteUnresolvedName`, for code whose scope is final.
    Bind node or failure to unresolved unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).

        // In a function body the scope is not final — but only a module may be left to the caller.
        If one's in-function:
            If one's checking-module is not "" and (name in lowercase) is not (one's checking-module in lowercase):
                Define needs as the entry for one's checking-module in one's module-needs but void is a series of text.
                Insert name into needs.
                In one's module-needs, the entry for one's checking-module becomes needs.
            Done.
            Define receiver as cast one's look-up on ("one").
            If receiver is not void:
                If receiver's shape's kind is "ObjectType":
                    Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (receiver's shape, 1)).
                    If cast one's field-type-of on (owner, name) is not void:
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                            "'{name}' is a field of '{owner}', and inside its methods a field is reached through 'one'", "",
                            at-row, "use '{name}' on its own",
                            "Write 'one's {name}' — 'one' is the {owner} the method was called on.")).
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            If cast one's is-module-name on (name) is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' isn't defined",
                    "A function or method uses the names it can see where it is WRITTEN — plus any module its caller pulled, and no module is named this",
                    at-row, "use '{name}' here",
                    "Define it first, take it as a parameter, or — if it is meant to be a module — declare it: 'Define object {name} with (...) and module:'.")).
            Done.
            If one's checking-module is not "", return cast unknown-type.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' isn't pulled here",
                "'{name}' is a module, and a function reaches one only where it is WRITTEN — a module's methods inherit what their caller pulled, but a plain function has no caller to inherit from",
                at-row, "use '{name}' inside this function without pulling it",
                "Pull it around the body: 'Pull a book on {name}. … Done.'")).
        Done.

        // A name that is a TYPE somewhere else is a different mistake from a missing variable.
        Define from-book as cast book-introducing on (name).
        If from-book is not "" and cast one's has-scoped-type on (name in lowercase):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is a type, and a type on its own isn't a value",
                "The '{from-book}' book IS pulled here, so the name is in scope — what is missing is the rest of the construction",
                at-row, "use '{name}' by itself where a value goes",
                "Give it the rest of what it is built from — see the '{from-book}' book in docs/BOOKS.md.")).
        Done.
        If from-book is not "":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is a type, and this program has not pulled it",
                "The '{from-book}' book introduces it, and the name means the type only inside that pull",
                at-row, "use '{name}' outside a '{from-book}' pull",
                "Wrap it in 'Pull a book on {from-book}. … Done.'")).
        Done.

        Define is-book as cast is-a-book on (name).
        Define ended-on as the entry for name in one's ended-names.
        // ⚠ Nested, not `is-book is false and ended-on is not void` — narrowing reads a lone
        // `is not void` test and does not see through `and`.
        If ended-on is not void:
            If is-book is false and ended-on is less than at-row:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' was defined on line {ended-on}, inside a block that has ended",
                    "A name lasts until the 'Done.' of the block it was defined in, and no further",
                    at-row, "use '{name}' after that block's 'Done.'",
                    "Use it before the 'Done.', or define it before the block begins so it outlasts it.")).
            Done.
        Done.

        If is-book:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is a book, and it is not pulled here",
                "A book's members can be used only inside 'Pull a book on {name}. … Done.', and the pull lasts until its 'Done.'",
                at-row, "use '{name}' outside a pull on it",
                "Put this line inside 'Pull a book on {name}.', before its 'Done.'.")).
        Done.

        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' isn't defined",
            "Nothing later in this block can give it a value — a name has to exist before it is used",
            at-row, "use '{name}' here",
            "Define it first: 'Define {name} as <value>.' — or check the spelling.")).
    Done.

    // ── Operators ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to infer-unary unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define op as cast field-of on (said, 1)'s word.
        Define operand as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define operand-kind as operand's kind.
        If operand-kind is "none", return operand.
        If op is "Not":
            If operand-kind is "FactType" or operand-kind is "BitsType", return operand.
            Define advice as "Make sure the value you're negating is a fact (a true or false value) or a bits value. Write a comparison like 'x is 5' if you need one.".
            If operand-kind is "NumberType":
                The advice becomes "A number is a quantity, and has no bits to flip. Write the value as a bit pattern (0xFF, 0b1010, 0o755) if that is what you meant, or use unary minus if you wanted to negate the quantity.".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'not' flips a fact or a bit pattern", "",
                at-row, "negate a {cast type-words on (operand)} value", advice)).
        Done.
        If operand-kind is "NumberType", return operand.
        Define advice as "Make sure the value you're negating is a number.".
        If operand-kind is "BitsType":
            The advice becomes "Bits are unsigned — a bit pattern has no negative. Did you mean 'not', which flips every bit within the value's width?".
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define union-fix as cast narrowing-fix on (cast field-of on (said, 2), operand, "NumberType").
            If union-fix is not "", the advice becomes union-fix.
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("unary minus works on numbers only", "",
            at-row, "negate a {cast type-words on (operand)} value", advice)).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-binary unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define lhs as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define op as cast field-of on (said, 2)'s word.
        Define rhs as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 4)).
        If lhs's kind is "none" or rhs's kind is "none", return cast unknown-type.
        Define lk as lhs's kind.
        Define rk as rhs's kind.

        // Matrix arithmetic comes first, as C# asks it before anything else.
        If op is "Plus" or op is "Minus" or op is "Star" or op is "Slash":
            Define matrix-result as cast one's matrix-arithmetic on (op, lhs, rhs, at-row, cast operator-words on (op)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (matrix-result) is false, return matrix-result.
        Done.

        // What this checker cannot weigh yet.
        For each seen in a series with (lhs, rhs), repeat:
            If cast beyond-types on (seen):
                Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("an operator on a {seen's kind}")).
            Done.
        Done.

        Define symbol as cast operator-words on (op).
        Define arithmetic as op is "Plus" or op is "Minus" or op is "Star" or op is "Slash" or op is "Percent".
        Define ordering as op is "Lt" or op is "Gt" or op is "Lte" or op is "Gte".
        Define gate as op is "And" or op is "Or" or op is "Xor".
        Define equality as op is "Equal" or op is "NotEqual".

        // A voidable number where a number goes, with a number on the other side too: say void.
        Define left-number as lk is "NumberType" or cast is-voidable-of on (lhs, "NumberType").
        Define right-number as rk is "NumberType" or cast is-voidable-of on (rhs, "NumberType").
        If (arithmetic or ordering) and left-number and right-number and (lk is "VoidableType" or rk is "VoidableType"):
            Define culprit as cast field-of on (said, 3).
            If lk is "VoidableType", the culprit becomes cast field-of on (said, 1).
            Define needs as "ordering needs a number that is there".
            Define action as "order a voidable number".
            If arithmetic:
                The needs becomes "{symbol} needs a number that is there".
                The action becomes "use {symbol} with a voidable number".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast void-misuse on (culprit, needs, action,
                "'({cast defaulted on (culprit, cast plain-type on ("NumberType"))})' in its place", at-row,
                "Keep the brackets: without them, the default runs on to the end of the line.")).
        Done.

        // A union where a number is needed: say how to find out which case it holds.
        Define number-fix as cast pair-narrowing-fix on (cast field-of on (said, 1), lhs, cast field-of on (said, 3), rhs, "NumberType").
        If arithmetic:
            If lk is "NumberType" and rk is "NumberType", return lhs.
            If lk is "BitsType" and rk is "BitsType", return lhs.
            Define fix as "If you meant arithmetic, both sides need to be numbers.\nIf you meant to join text, use 'joined to': \"hello\" joined to \" world\".".
            If number-fix is not "", the fix becomes number-fix.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("arithmetic requires numbers on both sides", "",
                at-row, "use {symbol} with {cast type-words on (lhs)} and {cast type-words on (rhs)}", fix)).
        Done.
        If equality:
            Define fact-type as cast plain-type on ("FactType").
            // A voidable against void, or against a plain value of what it holds.
            If (lk is "VoidableType" and rk is "VoidType") or (lk is "VoidType" and rk is "VoidableType"):
                Return fact-type.
            Done.
            If lk is "VoidableType":
                If cast same-type on (cast field-of on (lhs, 1), rhs), return fact-type.
            Done.
            If rk is "VoidableType":
                If cast same-type on (cast field-of on (rhs, 1), lhs), return fact-type.
            Done.
            If cast is-rabbit-type on (lhs) or cast is-rabbit-type on (rhs):
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a rabbit can't be compared, not even to another rabbit",
                    "A rabbit is a region with a lifetime of its own, not a value that can match another",
                    at-row, "compare a rabbit",
                    "Nothing tells one rabbit from another today. If you need that, it is worth asking for rather than working around.")).
            Done.
            If cast same-type on (lhs, rhs), return fact-type.
            // A union is compared with anything — legal before it is narrowed.
            If lk is "UnionType" or rk is "UnionType", return fact-type.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("equality comparison requires matching types", "",
                at-row, "compare a {cast type-words on (lhs)} to a {cast type-words on (rhs)}",
                "A {cast type-words on (lhs)} and a {cast type-words on (rhs)} can never be equal — this is likely a mistake. Check which side has the wrong type.")).
        Done.
        If ordering:
            If (lk is "NumberType" and rk is "NumberType") or (lk is "BitsType" and rk is "BitsType"):
                Return cast plain-type on ("FactType").
            Done.
            Define fix as "Ordering comparisons (>, <, >=, <=) need both sides to be numbers, or both to be bits.".
            If number-fix is not "", the fix becomes number-fix.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("ordering works on numbers and on bits", "",
                at-row, "order a {cast type-words on (lhs)} and a {cast type-words on (rhs)}", fix)).
        Done.
        If gate:
            If lk is "FactType" and rk is "FactType", return lhs.
            If lk is "BitsType" and rk is "BitsType", return lhs.
            If lk is "NumberType" or rk is "NumberType":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{symbol}' is a gate, and a number has no bits to combine", "",
                    at-row, "use '{symbol}' with {cast type-words on (lhs)} and {cast type-words on (rhs)}",
                    "Gates work on facts (one bit) and on bits (a pattern of them), not on numbers. A number is a quantity — 255 counts something, where 0xFF is a pattern of eight bits. Write the value as a bit pattern (0xFF, 0b1010, 0o755), or convert with 'converted to hex'.")).
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{symbol}' needs both sides to be the same kind of thing", "",
                at-row, "use '{symbol}' with {cast type-words on (lhs)} and {cast type-words on (rhs)}",
                "Both sides of '{symbol}' must be facts, or both must be bits. Did you mean to write a comparison like 'x is 0' rather than just 'x'?")).
        Done.
        Return cast unknown-type.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-voidable-of, given (the node shape, the text inner-kind):
        Return shape's kind is "VoidableType" and (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s kind is inner-kind.
    Done.

    // ── Text ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// What `converted to text` accepts — number, fact, text, bits and a chase.
    Bind fact to text-convertible, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        Return kind is "NumberType" or kind is "FactType" or kind is "TextType" or kind is "BitsType" or kind is "ChaseType".
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-join unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define lhs as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define rhs as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define place as 0.
        For each side-type in a series with (lhs, rhs), repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define side as cast field-of on (said, place).
            If side-type's kind is "VoidableType":
                Define inner as cast field-of on (side-type, 1).
                If cast text-convertible on (inner):
                    Define example as "'({cast defaulted on (side, inner)}) converted to text'".
                    If inner's kind is "TextType", the example becomes "'{cast defaulted on (side, inner)}'".
                    Return a failure (cast void-misuse on (side, "only text that is there can be joined",
                        "join a {cast type-words on (side-type)}", example, at-row, "")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (lhs) is false and lhs's kind is not "TextType":
            Define left-fix as cast narrowing-fix on (cast field-of on (said, 1), lhs, "TextType").
            If left-fix is not "":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you can only join text to text", "", at-row,
                    "join a {cast type-words on (lhs)} to text", left-fix)).
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you can only join text to text", "", at-row,
                "join a {cast type-words on (lhs)} to text",
                "Convert the {cast type-words on (lhs)} first: use 'converted to text'.\nFor example: n converted to text joined to \" items\".")).
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (rhs) is false and rhs's kind is not "TextType":
            Define right-fix as cast narrowing-fix on (cast field-of on (said, 2), rhs, "TextType").
            If right-fix is not "":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you can only join text to text", "", at-row,
                    "join text to a {cast type-words on (rhs)}", right-fix)).
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you can only join text to text", "", at-row,
                "join text to a {cast type-words on (rhs)}",
                "Convert the {cast type-words on (rhs)} first: use 'converted to text'.\nFor example: \"score: \" joined to n converted to text.")).
        Done.
        Return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-text-convert unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define value as cast field-of on (said, 1).
        Define operand as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        Define as-hole as cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (said, 4)).
        Define text-type as cast plain-type on ("TextType").
        If cast is-none on (operand) or cast text-convertible on (operand), return text-type.
        If operand's kind is "VoidableType":
            Define inner as cast field-of on (operand, 1).
            If cast text-convertible on (inner):
                Define action as "convert a {cast type-words on (operand)} to text".
                Define example as "'({cast defaulted on (value, inner)}) converted to text'".
                If as-hole:
                    The action becomes "put a {cast type-words on (operand)} in a hole".
                    The example becomes "'\{{cast defaulted on (value, inner)}\}'".
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast void-misuse on (value, "void has no text to convert to", action, example, at-row, "")).
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast beyond-types on (operand), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("converting a {operand's kind} to text")).
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'converted to text' doesn't work on {cast plural-words on (operand)}", "",
            at-row, "convert a {cast type-words on (operand)} to text",
            "Only numbers, facts, bits and a chase can be converted to text.")).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-number-convert unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define operand as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        If operand's kind is "BitsType", return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
        If cast is-none on (operand) is false and operand's kind is not "TextType":
            If cast beyond-types on (operand), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("converting a {operand's kind} to number")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'converted to number' expects text or bits", "", at-row,
                "convert a {cast type-words on (operand)} to number",
                "Text converts to a voidable number — void if it isn't a valid number. Bits convert to a plain number, since every bit pattern is some quantity.")).
        Done.
        Return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast plain-type on ("NumberType")).
    Done.

    /// A type around another — `(VoidableType (NumberType))`.
    Bind node to wrapped, given (the text kind, the node inner):
        Define shape as cast plain-type on (kind).
        Cast shape's add on (inner).
        Return shape.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-but-void unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define held as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define fallback as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        If held's kind is "VoidableType":
            Define inner as cast field-of on (held, 1).
            If cast is-none on (fallback) is false and cast assignable on (inner, fallback) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (fallback) or cast beyond-types on (inner), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a default of another kind")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "the default value is a {cast type-words on (fallback)}, but the voidable holds {cast plural-words on (inner)}", "",
                    at-row, "use a {cast type-words on (fallback)} as the default for a voidable {cast type-words on (inner)}",
                    "The default after 'but void is' must be a {cast type-words on (inner)}.")).
            Done.
            Return inner.
        Done.
        If held's kind is "VoidType", return fallback.
        If cast is-none on (held) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (held), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("'but void is' on a {held's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{cast type-words on (held)}' can never be void", "", at-row,
                "use 'but void is' on a {cast type-words on (held)} value",
                "Only voidable values can be void. 'but void is' is only needed for voidable values.")).
        Done.
        Return held.
    Done.

    // ── Series ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A written-out position that is not a whole number — C#'s `CheckIndex`.
    Bind void or failure to check-index, given (the node index-said, the number at-row):
        If index-said's kind is not "NumberLiteral", return.
        Define written as (cast field-of on (index-said, 1))'s word.
        Define amount as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (index-said, 1)).
        If amount % 1 is not 0:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("item positions must be whole numbers", "", at-row,
                "use {written} as a position", "Positions are counted 1, 2, 3 and so on. Use a whole number.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-series-literal unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define elements as cast field-of on (said, 1).
        Define annotation as cast field-of on (said, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define annotated as cast is-nothing on (annotation) is false.
        If annotated and cast beyond-types on (annotation), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a series annotated {annotation's kind}")).

        // A catalogue: its items need only fit the union, not match each other.
        If annotated and annotation's kind is "UnionType":
            For each element in elements's children, repeat:
                Define element-type as cast one's infer on (element) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-none on (element-type) is false and cast assignable on (annotation, element-type) is false:
                    If cast beyond-types on (element-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a catalogue item of a {element-type's kind}")).
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this item doesn't fit in a {cast type-words on (annotation)} collection",
                        "{cast type-words on (element-type)} is not one of the allowed types",
                        at-row, "add a {cast type-words on (element-type)} item",
                        "Only {cast type-words on (annotation)} values are allowed in this collection.")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", annotation).
        Done.

        Define inferred as cast unknown-type.
        Define place as 0.
        For each element in elements's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define element-type as cast one's infer on (element) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (element-type) is false:
                If cast is-none on (inferred):
                    The inferred becomes element-type.
                Done.
                Otherwise if cast same-type on (inferred, element-type) is false:
                    If cast beyond-types on (inferred) or cast beyond-types on (element-type):
                        Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a series of mixed kinds")).
                    Done.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("every item in a series must be the same type",
                        "The first item is a {cast type-words on (inferred)}, so all items must be {cast plural-words on (inferred)}",
                        at-row, "make item {place} a {cast type-words on (element-type)}",
                        "Remove the mismatched item, or define two separate series — one for {cast plural-words on (inferred)} and one for {cast plural-words on (element-type)}.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        If annotated:
            Cast one's check-resolves on (annotation) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (inferred) is false and cast same-type on (inferred, annotation) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (inferred), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a series of {inferred's kind}")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you said this is a series of {cast plural-words on (annotation)}",
                    "That annotation fixes the element type as {cast type-words on (annotation)}",
                    at-row, "put a {cast type-words on (inferred)} item in it",
                    "Fix the annotation to match the elements, or change the elements to match the annotation.")).
            Done.
            Return cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", annotation).
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (inferred):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("an empty series has no items to infer its type from", "",
                at-row, "define an empty series without saying what type of items it will hold",
                "Declare the element type: 'a series of numbers', 'a series of text', or 'a series of facts'.")).
        Done.
        Return cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", inferred).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-series-access unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define index-said as cast field-of on (said, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        If cast is-nothing on (index-said) is false:
            Cast check-index on (index-said, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define target as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If target's kind is "SeriesType", return cast field-of on (target, 1).
        If target's kind is "ChaseType", return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
        If target's kind is "RecordType":
            Return cast record-item on (target, cast field-of on (said, 1), index-said, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If target's kind is "ObjectType":
            Return cast one's object-item on (target, index-said, at-row, "access position") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If cast beyond-types on (target), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("an item of a {target's kind}")).
        Return cast unknown-type.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-series-length unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define counted as cast field-of on (said, 1).
        Define container as cast one's infer on (counted) or pass the failure off.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        If container's kind is "RecordType":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the number of' works on series, not records", "", at-row,
                "get the number of items in {cast expression-words on (counted)} (a record)",
                "Records don't have a length. Access individual fields by name or position.")).
        Done.
        If container's kind is "MapType":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the number of' works on series, not maps", "", at-row,
                "get the number of entries in {cast expression-words on (counted)} (a map)",
                "For maps, use 'the size of'. For text, use 'the length of'.")).
        Done.
        If container's kind is "TextType":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the number of' works on series, not text", "", at-row,
                "get the number of characters in {cast expression-words on (counted)} (a text)",
                "For text, use 'the length of'. For maps, use 'the size of'.")).
        Done.
        Return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
    Done.
Done.
